// Gather the per-agent companion windows on one niri workspace (issue #1306).
//
// The agents card's "Open terminals" button opens one `trollshell-agent-window`
// per running agent. On its own that gives you N windows wherever the
// compositor happens to put them; @kaesaecracker asked for them tiled together,
// which is these two nodes plus one config key.
//
// What each half does:
//
//   1. The plugin emits `niri msg action focus-workspace "hive"` BEFORE it
//      launches anything, so the windows open on the focused workspace and
//      niri tiles them there as columns — its own behaviour for new windows,
//      nothing further needed from us. This half needs `niri` on the plugin's
//      PATH and nothing in this file.
//
//   2. The window rule below sends every agent window there regardless of
//      what is focused — so a single pill click lands on the same workspace,
//      and so does a window opened while you were somewhere else.
//
// ⚠️ The workspace name MUST equal `window.workspace` in
// `~/.config/trollshell/agents.toml` (default `"hive"`). They are two spellings
// of one place and nothing checks them against each other: a mismatch focuses
// an empty workspace and opens the windows on another one, which looks exactly
// like the feature not working.
//
// niri has no `include` directive, so merge these two top-level nodes into your
// `~/.config/niri/config.kdl` by hand — anywhere at the top level, next to your
// other `workspace` / `window-rule` nodes. niri reloads on save.

// A named workspace, so it exists before anything opens on it and keeps its
// place in the order. The block is where an `open-on-output "DP-2"` would go if
// you want the agents on a particular monitor.
workspace "hive" {}

// Every agent window, by the app-id prefix `cli::app_id` builds
// (`mov.vibec0re.trollshell.AgentWindow.<agent>`) — one rule for all of them.
// The raw kdl string is so the regex's backslashes reach the regex engine
// rather than being eaten as kdl escapes; the trailing `\.` is what stops the
// pattern from also matching a future `…AgentWindowSomethingElse`.
window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^mov\.vibec0re\.trollshell\.AgentWindow\."#
    open-on-workspace "hive"
}
